<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!-- MISSION: Task 3 - GPS waypoint (GUIDED), then MANUAL: slide to the first GREEN bay, close in, pan/tilt cannon. -->
<!--
  task3_scan_fire.xml - Task 3 in one run (the body is lib/task3_scan_fire.xml, Task3ScanFire, which
  mission_t1_t3_t4.xml runs after Task 1), from the GCS with an APPROACH POINT (the Run
  box's approach lat/lon: a few metres in front of the dock) and a long timeout (3600 s).

    camera: SetCameraModel puts camera_node on the dock model and waits until it sees with
       it. A camera restart comes back on buoy, which never sees the dock.
    0. GUIDED to the approach point (skipped when the run starts in MANUAL;
       cut short, the run going on, when the pilot switches to MANUAL mid-leg).
    1. the tree switches GUIDED -> MANUAL itself (only from GUIDED; SC still takes it back).
    2. SEARCH: turn to the dock heading, slide one way (the Run panel's "slide first", else
       left) along the dock until a bay
       the camera sees reads GREEN with confidence (CommitFirstGreen: the first one, not every bay; numbered
       left to right for the docking report).
    From GREEN on, two branches side by side (Parallel):
    3. APPROACH: square to the dock heading, strafe the GREEN bay's FACE onto the bow's
       line (the indicator only says which bay; its spot kept on the map, so a few lost frames do not stop it), then a
       steady, gently ramped push straight in (ApproachBay), to 2.0 m and centred.
    4. HOLD: the camera 1.7 m off the face (its depth), the face centred, square
       (StrafeKeep). The docking report goes the FIRST time the boat is in close (the face
       1.3-2.1 m off the camera, within 0.30 m of the bow's line, within 10 deg of square:
       hold_s 0); nothing is checked after it, the hold only keeps the bay in front of the cannon.
    5. THE FIRE, in a loop, docked or not: a window of our bay reads RED -> the cannon
       sprays it, water on until it reads GREEN (and on through drop-outs of up to 5 s)
       -> BACK OFF: the hold moves out to t3_backoff_m off the face (the GCS Run panel's
       "back off", bt_runner_node t3_backoff_m, 4 m when unset), still centred and square
       -> firefighting report -> the 2-colour code (read from out there) -> resource
       delivery report -> wait for the next RED; a new RED brings the hold back in to 1.7 m.
       At the competition the light comes on only after step 4.

  TASK 4 (Disruptive, task4_leaves.cpp): AvoidInvaders round the body. No moving object
  reported or none coming at the boat: it is invisible. One coming: the body is halted, the boat
  goes GUIDED (asked for from MANUAL) and gets out of its way, comes back, asks for MANUAL again
  and the body starts over: the bay is kept, and the cannon fires again only on a new RED.
  IsAutonomous manual="true" over it ends the run in HOLD or with the autonomy-drop latch (SC)
  set, as the body's own guards do, also while an escape has the body halted.

  RoboCommand (via ocs_client and the OCS): the heartbeat says TASK_COORDINATED_LOGISTICS
  while this runs (TaskAttempt). The docking report names the bay, and RoboCommand lights
  a window in THAT bay: the number is the layout's when all three bays are known, else a
  guess from the bays seen either side and the slide direction (start at the dock's right
  end when sliding left). The indicator colour comes from the classifier (indicator="yolo";
  task3_scan_fire_cv reads it by colour thresholds).

  THE DOCK DETECTOR: the new one, models/ffcv/best.pt (dock_weights=""). The same run on the
  Oct 3 detector is task3_scan_fire_old_dock.xml: pick that mission in the GCS instead.
-->
<root BTCPP_format="4" main_tree_to_execute="ScanFire">
  <include path="lib/task3_scan_fire.xml"/>

  <BehaviorTree ID="ScanFire">
    <!-- the heartbeat's current_task (handbook 3.4.11): TASK_COORDINATED_LOGISTICS from
         the first tick, TASK_NONE when the run ends; RoboCommand starts Task 3's
         attempt on it -->
    <TaskAttempt token="TASK_COORDINATED_LOGISTICS">
      <ReactiveSequence name="guard_band">
        <IsAutonomous manual="true"/>
        <AvoidInvaders>
          <SubTree ID="Task3ScanFire" _autoremap="true" dock_weights=""/>
        </AvoidInvaders>
      </ReactiveSequence>
    </TaskAttempt>
  </BehaviorTree>
</root>
